---
import Content from '../../layouts/Content.astro';
import { site } from '../../config';

const { metaPixelId, brevo } = site.marketing;
---

<Content
  title="Privacy notice | dhobermans"
  description="How dhobermans handles the details you share when you book a laundry pickup: what stays on your device and what goes into your WhatsApp message."
  h1="Privacy notice"
  lead="What we collect, why, and the choices you have."
  flow="question"
  cta="Ask us a question"
>
  <p class="note">Last updated: 15 November 2026</p>

  <h2>Who we are</h2>
  <p>
    dhobermans is a laundry pickup and delivery service based in {site.base.full}. You can reach us on WhatsApp at {site.whatsappDisplay}.
  </p>

  <h2>Details you enter when booking</h2>
  <p>
    The booking form builds a WhatsApp message from what you type: your name, address, pincode, chosen services, pickup time and any notes. You
    see the full message before anything is sent, and it is sent by you, from your own WhatsApp, when you tap send. We use it to arrange your
    pickup and delivery and to reply to you. WhatsApp is provided by Meta and is covered by WhatsApp's own privacy policy.
  </p>

  <h2>What is saved on your device</h2>
  <p>
    To make repeat bookings quicker, your name, address, pincode, map pin, last order and shopping cart are saved in your browser's storage on
    your own device. They are not uploaded to us. You can remove them with "Forget my saved details" in the dhobermans app menu, or by clearing
    this site's data in your browser.
  </p>

  <h2>Location and maps</h2>
  <p>
    Your location is read only when you tap the button to share it. It is used to check your distance from us and is added to your WhatsApp
    message as a map link so our rider can find you. If you open the map, map images are loaded from OpenStreetMap, which receives your IP
    address in the way any website does.
  </p>

  <h2>Campaign references</h2>
  <p>
    If you arrive through an advert or a tagged link, we remember the campaign name on your device for up to 30 days and add a short reference
    line to your WhatsApp message, so we know which campaigns work.
  </p>

  {
    metaPixelId && (
      <>
        <h2>Meta (Facebook and Instagram) advertising</h2>
        <p>
          We use the Meta Pixel and Meta's Conversions API to measure our adverts. Meta receives page visits and booking events together with
          your IP address, browser details and Meta's cookie identifiers. If you choose to receive offers from us, a hashed (scrambled) version
          of your mobile number and first name is included so Meta can match the event. The Pixel is not loaded when your browser sends a Global
          Privacy Control or Do Not Track signal.
        </p>
      </>
    )
  }

  {
    brevo && (
      <>
        <h2>Offers and reminders</h2>
        <p>
          If you tick the box to receive offers and pickup reminders, your mobile number and first name are stored with our messaging provider,
          Brevo, and used only to send you those messages. It is optional, and you can stop at any time by replying to a message or telling us on
          WhatsApp.
        </p>
      </>
    )
  }

  <h2>Hosting</h2>
  <p>
    This website is delivered by Cloudflare, which processes technical data such as your IP address to serve pages and keep the site secure.
  </p>

  <h2>Your choices</h2>
  <p>
    We do not sell your personal information. To see, correct or delete the details we hold about you, or to stop marketing messages, message us
    on WhatsApp at {site.whatsappDisplay}.
  </p>
</Content>
